content.text:
verdict: clean
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1, result: pass, notes: "Diagram and skill walk step-for-step against the steps section — all nine steps, all four prompts verbatim, all six branch rows with matching labels and conditions, repaired inputs (glossary on draft, round on route-approval) present in both renderings; diagram states 'Generated from the steps below... do not edit by hand' and the skill declares generated: true / generated-by / source-digest."}
  - {scenario: 2, result: pass, notes: "O1 → draft.checks (set.scope == scope) plus scenarios scored in screen-read; O2 → log-round's round_log append plus fresh-context: true on screen-read; O3 → route-approval's branches, where end is reachable only via the owner's approving verdict or park; O4 → both labeled failsafe branches plus park.run filing the finding — every witness exists and is decidable from the run record."}
  - {scenario: 3, result: pass, notes: "Inner cycle (screen-read → route-verdict → revise) has labeled success exit 'clean or tradeoffs accepted' and cap round >= 3; outer cycle (authority-approve → route-approval → revise) has labeled success exit 'owner approves' and cap round >= 6; round advances on every revise, so neither cycle can run unbounded."}
  - {scenario: 4, result: pass, notes: "Every prompt/check/run reference resolves to a declared name: draft reads sources/scope/guideline_paths/glossary, screen-read reads set/fitness_path, revise reads set/review/guideline_paths, park templates only scope/round/review; authority-approve's 'hold-after' points at this definition's own frontmatter field and describes run lifecycle rather than directing a context load."}
  - {scenario: 5, result: pass, notes: "result: set (principle-set) matches the purpose ('Author or amend a principle set') and the frontmatter produces: [principle-set] — the run returns the artifact it exists to produce."}
  - {scenario: 6, result: pass, notes: "All step prose sits in prompt fields — runtime steps carry only set/branches/run structures and short branch labels; the guiding statement ('the statement decides, the rationale evidences, the implications price — never on taste') is a cross-step judgment about the artifact, not a step sequence."}
stumbles: ["Silence holds the run after the declared window — `hold-after` in this definition's frontmatter — the one prompt reference that resolves to frontmatter rather than a step input; decidable, but it made me stop and hunt", "The compiled skill prints 'writes: —' for runtime steps (log-round, advance-round) whose yaml immediately shows a `set:` clause writing a value — the summary line contradicts the block under it", "O1's witness 'fitness scenarios 1 and 5' points into ../fitness/principle-set.fitness.md, which a reader of this file alone cannot confirm covers four-part form and screen coverage"]
top_changes: ["Have the compiler render set-clause targets in the runtime steps' 'writes:' summary line instead of '—'", "Move the hold-window sentence in authority-approve's prompt to step-record metadata or the definition prose, so prompts reference only declared step inputs", "Quote or name the two witnessed assertions in O1 (four-part form; screen coverage) so the outcome is checkable without opening the principle-set fitness file"]
